From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd: keep the laddr out of the data format bits

The first byte of SLIM_USR_MC_DEF_ACT_CHAN is the channel's data format
in its top three bits and the client's number in the low five. Every
downstream NGD driver builds it that way:

	wbuf[txn.len++] = (u8) (slc->prop.dataf << 5) | (sb->laddr & 0x1f);

This one sent the whole logical address. Satellite addresses have the top
bits set (the WCD9320 on the Xperia Z1 Compact is 0xcb), so the manager
was asked for a channel of data format 6, not "not defined".

---
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,9 @@
 		if (txn.msg->num_bytes == 0) {
 			int exp = 0, coef = 0;
 
-			wbuf[txn.msg->num_bytes++] = sdev->laddr;
+			/* the top three bits are the data format; only five for the client */
+			wbuf[txn.msg->num_bytes++] = port->ch.data_fmt << 5 |
+						      (sdev->laddr & 0x1f);
 			wbuf[txn.msg->num_bytes] = rt->bps >> 2 |
 						   (port->ch.aux_fmt << 6);
 
